  "question": {
    "text": "Consider the combination of two&nbsp;capacitors <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>, with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>, when connected in parallel, the equivalent capacitance is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math> times the equivalent capacitance of the same connected in series. Calculate the ratio of capacitors, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></math>.",
